WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.738
Welcome back to your Danish citizenship exam companion.

2
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:07.080
This is Chapter Six, Episode Seven, Part Two.

3
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.530
Greenland's self-government.

4
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.143
Until 1953, Greenland was a colony under Denmark.

5
00:00:14.143 --> 00:00:23.655
With the constitutional amendment in 1953, Greenland came under the constitution on an equal footing with Denmark and the Faroe Islands.

6
00:00:23.655 --> 00:00:30.780
Greenland and Denmark agreed in 1978 to establish home rule, hjemmestyre, for Greenland.

7
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:50.805
After a referendum, Greenland got home rule by law in 1979, which meant that Greenland gradually in the following years took over responsibility for, and the possibility of passing its own laws in, a number of areas, for example social policy, taxes and duties, and education.

8
00:00:50.805 --> 00:01:02.405
In 2009 the home rule arrangement was replaced by a self-government arrangement, selvstyre, which gave Greenland the possibility of getting self-determination in even more areas.

9
00:01:02.405 --> 00:01:09.767
This applies, among other things, to the legal system and the management of resources and raw materials in the subsoil.

10
00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:17.442
It was also established that the Greenlanders are a people in their own right with title to full independence when they themselves wish it.

11
00:01:17.992 --> 00:01:24.492
Greenland's national day is the 21st of June, because it is the year's longest and brightest day.

12
00:01:24.442 --> 00:01:36.942
The self-government arrangement therefore came into force on the 21st of June 2009, and the Greenlandic flag was hoisted for the first time on the 21st of June 1985.

13
00:01:36.942 --> 00:01:41.580
It is called in Greenlandic Erfalasorput, which means "our flag".

14
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.042
The flag's colours are red and white as in Dannebrog.

15
00:01:45.042 --> 00:01:50.242
The circle in the flag symbolises the rising sun in the white Greenlandic landscape.

16
00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:53.124
The flag is widely used in Greenland.

17
00:01:53.674 --> 00:02:06.287
The self-government consists of Greenland's parliament, Inatsisartut, which is an elected and legislative assembly, and an administration led by Greenland's government, Naalakkersuisut.

18
00:02:06.237 --> 00:02:10.712
The government corresponds to a government and has the political leadership.

19
00:02:10.712 --> 00:02:15.324
The parliament has 31 members, elected for four years at a time.

20
00:02:15.324 --> 00:02:18.449
The chair of the government is elected by the parliament.

21
00:02:18.449 --> 00:02:23.124
The parliament passes the laws in all areas the self-government has taken over.

22
00:02:23.124 --> 00:02:37.782
These include social services, education, health service, taxes and duties, housing, commercial fishing and hunting, raw materials, municipal matters, environment, culture and leisure, and infrastructure.

23
00:02:38.332 --> 00:02:49.557
Greenland receives in 2025 an economic grant from the Danish state of a little over four billion kroner a year, which covers a good half of the self-government's expenses.

24
00:02:49.507 --> 00:02:55.857
Fishing, especially of shrimp, is the most important export income source for Greenlandic society.

25
00:02:55.857 --> 00:03:05.282
With the self-government arrangement from 2009 it was established that income from raw material activities in Greenland goes to Greenland's self-government.

26
00:03:05.282 --> 00:03:11.952
At the same time it was decided that such income should lead to a reduction in the Danish state's grant to Greenland.

27
00:03:12.502 --> 00:03:16.102
The main industries in Greenland are fishing and tourism.

28
00:03:16.052 --> 00:03:22.914
The traditional trapper trade, where people lived by catching not least seals, is by contrast dying out.

29
00:03:22.914 --> 00:03:35.610
Greenland became, as part of the Kingdom of Denmark, a member of the EF, now the EU, in 1973, but after a referendum in Greenland was withdrawn again in 1985.

30
00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.272
Greenland's cultural life.

31
00:03:38.222 --> 00:03:44.360
Greenland has a rich cultural life, which stretches from traditional drum dance to modern rock music.

32
00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:48.510
The age-old Greenlandic legends are written down and taught in schools.

33
00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:56.124
In addition there is a widespread production of handicrafts carved from bones and teeth of the animals in and around Greenland.

34
00:03:56.674 --> 00:04:06.624
Hans Lynge, who lived from 1906 to 88, is regarded as one of the most significant personalities within Greenlandic visual art and literature.

35
00:04:06.574 --> 00:04:15.611
Hans Lynge was also politically active, a critic of Denmark's influence on Greenland, and a champion of greater Greenlandic independence.

36
00:04:15.611 --> 00:04:23.061
His art is marked by a strong love for the original Greenlandic cultural heritage and the Inuit's traditional way of life.

37
00:04:23.061 --> 00:04:35.118
He is especially known for the novel Ersinngitsup piumasaa, "The Will of the Invisible", from 1938, which is about revenge and the conflict between traditional honour and modern conscience.

38
00:04:35.668 --> 00:04:49.368
In 2021 the Greenlandic author Niviaq Korneliussen, born 1990, received the Nordic Council's Literature Prize for the novel Naasuliardarpi, "Valley of Flowers", from 2020.

39
00:04:49.318 --> 00:05:00.868
The book is about social and psychological problems among young Greenlanders and their feeling of belonging neither in traditional Greenlandic culture nor in a modern big city like Copenhagen.

40
00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:08.184
And about the inability and unwillingness of politicians, authorities, families and friends to help them.

41
00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:12.359
Christianity plays a significant role in Greenland.

42
00:05:12.309 --> 00:05:18.934
The church in Greenland is part of the Danish national church, but belongs under Greenland's self-government.

43
00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:20.909
Greenland has its own bishop.

44
00:05:20.909 --> 00:05:29.346
The church service in Greenland takes place in Greenlandic, and a special Greenlandic tradition has developed for how hymns are sung in the churches.

45
00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:32.321
Here is your recap for Episode Seven.

46
00:05:32.271 --> 00:05:43.808
The realm community's official name is Kongeriget Danmark; the constitution applies in all three parts; Greenland and the Faroe Islands each elect two members of the Folketing.

47
00:05:43.808 --> 00:05:49.171
Foreign and security policy and monetary policy are decided by Denmark.

48
00:05:49.171 --> 00:05:56.908
In 2005, Greenland and the Faroe Islands got the possibility to negotiate certain international agreements.

49
00:05:56.908 --> 00:06:04.446
Greenland is the world's largest island, 2.1 million square kilometres, 98 percent of the realm.

50
00:06:04.446 --> 00:06:14.496
About 83 percent, so roughly 80 percent, is covered by ice all year; the Inland Ice is up to 3,400 metres thick.

51
00:06:14.496 --> 00:06:20.183
The highest point is Gunnbjørn Fjeld, 3,694 metres.

52
00:06:20.183 --> 00:06:24.183
About 57,000 live there, about 20,000 in Nuuk.

53
00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:27.046
The Inuit immigrated about 1200.

54
00:06:27.046 --> 00:06:32.683
Hans Egede came in 1721 and founded Godthåb in 1728.

55
00:06:32.683 --> 00:06:38.683
The Royal Greenland Trading Department had its monopoly from 1776 to 1950.

56
00:06:38.683 --> 00:06:43.883
In 1941, Henrik Kauffmann made the agreement with the USA.

57
00:06:43.883 --> 00:06:50.246
Thule, in the early 1950s, was renamed Pituffik Space Base in 2023.

58
00:06:50.246 --> 00:07:05.683
Greenland was a colony until 1953; home rule was agreed in 1978 and came into force in 1979; self-government came on the 21st of June 2009, which is also Greenland's national day.

59
00:07:05.683 --> 00:07:12.021
The flag Erfalasorput was first hoisted on the 21st of June 1985.

60
00:07:12.021 --> 00:07:15.458
The parliament Inatsisartut has 31 members.

61
00:07:15.458 --> 00:07:20.183
The Danish grant in 2025 is a little over four billion kroner.

62
00:07:20.183 --> 00:07:26.358
Fishing, especially shrimp, is the main export, and fishing and tourism are the main industries.

63
00:07:26.358 --> 00:07:29.346
Greenland left the EF in 1985.

64
00:07:29.346 --> 00:07:34.971
Today neither Greenland nor the Faroe Islands is part of the EU, although Denmark is.

65
00:07:34.971 --> 00:07:39.684
Greenland's church is part of the Danish national church, with its own bishop.

66
00:07:40.234 --> 00:07:42.834
Now it is time for your exam practice.

67
00:07:42.784 --> 00:07:47.696
These are real questions from past Danish citizenship exams on what you just heard.

68
00:07:47.696 --> 00:07:55.182
For each one, I will read the question and the choices, then pause so you can pick your answer, and then I will give you the correct answer.

69
00:07:55.732 --> 00:07:56.982
Question 1.

70
00:07:56.932 --> 00:08:00.132
When did the law on home rule in Greenland come into force?

71
00:08:00.132 --> 00:08:02.657
Option A: 1949.

72
00:08:02.657 --> 00:08:05.357
Option B: 1979.

73
00:08:05.357 --> 00:08:07.608
Option C: 2009.
[DA] Hvornår trådte loven om hjemmestyre i Grønland i kraft?  A: 1949  |  B: 1979  |  C: 2009

74
00:08:14.158 --> 00:08:17.195
The answer is B: 1979.

75
00:08:17.145 --> 00:08:21.378
It appeared in the November 2020 and June 2021 exams.
[DA] ✔ B: 1979

76
00:08:21.928 --> 00:08:23.178
Question 2.

77
00:08:23.128 --> 00:08:26.040
Are Greenland and the Faroe Islands part of the EU?

78
00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.665
Option A: Yes.

79
00:08:27.665 --> 00:08:29.316
Option B: No.
[DA] Er Grønland og Færøerne en del af EU?  A: Ja  |  B: Nej

80
00:08:35.866 --> 00:08:37.866
The answer is B: No.

81
00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:42.174
It appeared in the November 2022 and May 2025 exams.
[DA] ✔ B: Nej

82
00:08:42.724 --> 00:08:44.061
Question 3.

83
00:08:44.011 --> 00:08:46.536
Which symbol is part of Greenland's flag?

84
00:08:46.536 --> 00:08:48.736
Option A: A cross.

85
00:08:48.736 --> 00:08:51.049
Option B: A triangle.

86
00:08:51.049 --> 00:08:53.280
Option C: A circle.
[DA] Hvilket symbol indgår i Grønlands flag?  A: Et kors  |  B: En trekant  |  C: En cirkel

87
00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:02.142
The answer is C: A circle.

88
00:09:02.092 --> 00:09:06.402
It appeared in the May 2024 and November 2025 exams.
[DA] ✔ C: En cirkel

89
00:09:06.952 --> 00:09:08.714
That's the end of this part.

90
00:09:08.664 --> 00:09:09.732
Well done.

